"Logos - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki/Logos)\nciteturn38search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; > Live dashboard: logos.modelmarket.dev · Landing: alexar76.github.io/logos · Source: github.com/alexar76/logos\n\n# Logos - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki\n\n# LOGOS — federation analytics\n\nLOGOS is the ecosystem's read-only federation analytics engine. It takes real Hub snapshots and measured settlement volume, runs rolling z-score anomaly detection, correlates across sources, and answers natural-language questions through Metis — without inventing zeros for missing data.\n\n> Live dashboard: logos.modelmarket.dev · Landing: alexar76.github.io/logos · Source: github.com/alexar76/logos\n\n## Why LOGOS matters in AICOM\n\nLayer  | Role\n--- | ---\nHub / peers  | Live catalog, invoke routes, settlement telemetry\nMOMUS / SKOPOS / Treasury  | Security findings, fleet posture, bounty pay — polled as sources\nLOGOS  | Observatory — snapshots, anomalies, cross-source insights, guarded assistant\nMetis  | Optional NL reasoning behind insights (fail-closed when unreachable)\n\nHard invariant: LOGOS is read-only by construction. It does not scan, remediate, pay, or deploy. An unreachable source stays `unavailable` / `—`, never a fake `0`.\n\n## What operators get\n\n  * Real Hub snapshots + measured settlement volume (not projected)\n  * Rolling z-score anomalies and cross-source correlations\n  * Natural-language insights (Metis) + a guarded chat surface\n  * 5-language UI; SQLite or Postgres store\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLOGOS — Federation Analytics Engine (https://alexar76.github.io/logos/)\nciteturn38search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Read-only analytics over the AIMarket federation — measured settlement-volume projections, catalog pricing, rolling z-score anomaly detection, Metis-assisted insights, and a prompt-injection-guarded assistant.\n\n🟢 Live demo GitHub ↗ Documentation ↗ ... logos.modelmarket.dev is live.\nLOGOS\n\nHome Analytics NEXUS AI Assistant Consumption\n\n[Button: EN] [Button: RU] [Button: ES] [Button: FR] [Button: 中文]\n\nFederation intelligence / live\n\n# LOGOS\n\nOne node. Every insight.\nRead-only analytics over the AIMarket federation — measured settlement-volume projections, catalog pricing, rolling z-score anomaly detection, Metis-assisted insights, and a prompt-injection-guarded assistant.\n\n🟢 Live demo GitHub ↗ Documentation ↗\n\nPart of the AICOM ecosystem · monorepo · MIT\n\n16 ENDPOINTS LIVE TELEMETRY\n\nMETIS COUNCIL NL INSIGHT LAYER\n\nROLLING Z-SCORE ANOMALY METHOD\n\n## 🚀 Try it now\n\nlogos.modelmarket.dev is live. Ask about the federation, explore capabilities via NEXUS, inspect measured settlement and catalog pricing, or chat with the AI assistant.\n\n📊 Dashboard ↗ 🧿 NEXUS ↗ 🤖 AI Chat ↗\n\n6\n\nDashboard Views\n\n16\n\nAPI Endpoints\n\n5\n\nLanguages\n\n80\n\nTests\n\n3D\n\nConstellation\n\n## 📊 Insights & Analytics\n\nNatural-language queries answered from live federation data. Professional charts, sortable tables, heatmaps.\n\n### Federation Insights\n\nAsk \"How long will Treasury last?\", \"Which hub is slow?\", \"Any critical findings?\" — typed answers with severity, sources, and recommendations.\n\neconomy security latency reputation\n\nOpen Insights ↗\n\n### Analytics Dashboard\n\nLine charts (24h trends), bar charts (per-hub), donut charts (severity), heatmap calendar (90-day anomaly activity), sortable+groupable data tables.\n\nline bar donut heatmap\n\nOpen Analytics ↗\n\n### 3D Constellation\n\nThe federation as a living starfield — hub nodes as pulsing orbs, connection trails, anomaly rings. Interactive Three.js visualization.\n\nthree.js 3D WebGL\n\nOpen Insights ↗\n\n## 🧿 NEXUS — Federation Playground\n\nSelect any capability from the catalog, craft JSON input, invoke — and see the routing trace, price, and verifiable result.\n\n### Capability Browser\n\nFull catalog of every capability across the federation — names, descriptions, prices, provider hubs. Drop-down selector with live refresh.\n\nOpen NEXUS ↗\n\n### Manual Invoke\n\nCraft JSON input, hit INVOKE, and see the result. Routing trace shows which hub served the request, price charged, and verifiable proof.\n\nTry it ↗\n\n## 🤖 AI Assistant\n\nChat with the LOGOS assistant. Full read-only access to the analytics store. Prompt-injection guarded. Multi-provider LLM support. Voice input.\n\n### Multi-Provider LLM\n\nDeepSeek V4 Pro (default), Anthropic Claude, OpenAI, Ollama, LM Studio — same named presets as MOMUS. Switch provider, model, base URL via env vars.\n\ndeepseek claude openai ollama\n\nGitHub ↗\n\n### Input Guard\n\nWarden-style deterministic prompt-injection filter — blocks prompt extraction, role-switching, token smuggling, and delimiter injection before reaching the LLM.\n\nprompt-injection deterministic\n\nOpen AI Chat ↗\n\n## 💰 Consumption Tracking\n\nMeasured 24-hour settlement volume, 30-day projection only when that measurement exists, catalog pricing by hub, and CSV export. Missing telemetry remains unavailable—not zero.\n\nLOGOS — the analytical brain of the AICOM open agent economy\n\nMIT · Python 3.11+ · FastAPI · React · Three.js · 80 tests · 16 API endpoints · 6 dashboard views--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHome - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki)\nciteturn38search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Ecosystem landing  | alexar76.github.io/aicom · modeldev.modelmarket.dev ... Metis (cognition): metis.modelmarket.dev · Metis · LOGOS (analytics): logos.modelmarket.dev · Logos\n\n# Home - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki\n\n# AI-Factory — Wiki\n\nSelf-hosted MIT factory: plain-language idea → multi-agent pipeline → shippable web product (landing or full stack).\nLive demo  | magic-ai-factory.com\nEcosystem landing  | alexar76.github.io/aicom · modeldev.modelmarket.dev\nDemo admin  | admin/login — passwordless (`admin`, Enter admin demo) (demo host only)\nDemo disclaimer  | Shared site — `AIFACTORY_DEMO_READONLY=1` blocks settings save, backup/restore, user CRUD\nSource repo  | github.com/alexar76/aicom\nEcosystem knowledge base  | `docs/ecosystem/knowledge-base.md` · whitepaper\nFull docs in tree  | `docs/` (50+ guides)\nYouTube  | Idea → agents → shippable product\n\n## What it is\n\nAI-Factory is a multi-agent pipeline you run on your own server: analyst, PM, architect, developer, QA/E2E, security, DevOps, marketing, and more. State and artifacts live on disk (`data/`), you bring your own LLM keys, and there is no per-seat cloud pricing.\n\nTypical wall-clock (DeepSeek, without long repair loops): marketing_landing ~20–25 min; full_software ~25–45 min for a simple brief, up to hours when gates iterate.\n\n## Quick start (self-hosted)\n    \n    `git clone https://github.com/alexar76/aicom.git\n    cd aicom && cp -n .env.example .env\n    docker compose up -d --build\n    # UI → http://localhost:9080/admin/login\n    `\n\nThere is no default admin password in the repo — see Security and `docs/security.md`.\n\nMore detail: Quick-Start · Quick-Start-Ecosystem (full fleet) · Deployment\n\n## Role in the AICOM ecosystem\n\nThe public factory repo (alexar76/aicom) ships AI-Factory (pipeline + storefront). The wider AIMarket stack lives in sibling satellites: hub, protocol, desktop SKUs, plugins, widget, SDKs, oracles, GAIA/ATLAS, Metis, LOGOS, SKOPOS, MOMUS/Treasury, Signal Hunt, DIOSCURI/HELIOS/THEOROS, ACEX, mesh, and MCP servers.\n\nThe factory produces shippable products and machine-readable capabilities; the hub indexes, routes, and settles them for desktop apps, widgets, and autonomous agents. Auto-Mesh Pipeline — a run can discover peer agents on the hub, pay via channel, invoke them, and ship a connected product.\n\nFull map: Ecosystem · Oracles · Metis · Logos · Signal-Hunt · `docs/ecosystem/knowledge-base.md`